Dear {mpName},

Our community in {riding} is ready to welcome Teo Castell, and I am writing as a constituent to ask for your help getting his application moving. Teo is stateless, and Northbridge Newcomer Alliance, a nonprofit based here in our riding, is sponsoring him.

The Alliance submitted his complete permanent residence application through private sponsorship. Eleven months later it is still in security screening, with no additional information provided. Since March 2026, housing and settlement support have been waiting for him.

Teo has never held citizenship anywhere. He has no passport and lives in Lisbon on a temporary humanitarian permit that he must renew every year. No other country is waiting to take him in.

As our MP, please contact Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada and the Minister of Immigration’s office to ask about the status of his application and to have it reviewed as soon as possible.

Sincerely,

{firstName} {lastName}
{street}
{city}, {province} {postalCode}

Dear {mpName},

I am a constituent of {riding}, and I am asking for your help with the permanent residence application of Teo Castell, a stateless man privately sponsored by Northbridge Newcomer Alliance, a Canadian nonprofit.

Teo has never had a country. Born stateless, he holds no passport and no citizenship, and he lives in Lisbon on a temporary humanitarian permit renewed each year. His complete application was submitted through private sponsorship, yet it has been in security screening for 11 months, and no additional information has been provided.

His sponsors have had housing and settlement support ready since March 2026. Without citizenship, he cannot travel freely, work securely, or plan a future, and each month of waiting is another month without protection.

Please contact Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada and the Minister of Immigration’s office to ask for the status of his application and to have it reviewed as soon as possible. I would be grateful to hear back from your office.

Sincerely,

{firstName} {lastName}
{street}
{city}, {province} {postalCode}

Dear {mpName},

I am writing as a constituent of {riding} because Teo Castell, a stateless man, has been waiting 11 months for Canada to finish screening his application. Northbridge Newcomer Alliance, a Canadian nonprofit, is privately sponsoring him, and I am asking for your help to move his case forward.

His permanent residence application was submitted complete. It has sat in security screening ever since, and no additional information has been provided.

Teo has no passport and no citizenship anywhere. He lives in Lisbon on a temporary humanitarian permit that he must renew each year. Meanwhile, his sponsors have had housing and settlement support ready since March 2026.

We must stand by people with no country to call home. Every month of delay is another month without protection.

Please contact Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada and the Minister of Immigration’s office about the status of his application and ask that it be reviewed as soon as possible.

Sincerely,

{firstName} {lastName}
{street}
{city}, {province} {postalCode}

Dear {mpName},

I am writing to ask for your help. Northbridge Newcomer Alliance, a Canadian nonprofit, is privately sponsoring Teo Castell, a stateless man, and his application has stalled. I am a constituent of {riding}.

Teo’s complete permanent residence application has been in security screening for 11 months. No additional information has been provided.

